+    }
+
+    h1 {
+      margin: 0 0 12px;
+      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.3rem);
+      line-height: 1.05;
+    }
+
+    .intro {
+      margin: 0;
+      color: var(--muted);
+      line-height: 1.65;
+      max-width: 62ch;
+    }
+
+    .faq {
+      display: grid;
+      gap: 14px;
+    }
+
+    .example {
+      border: 1px solid var(--border);
+      border-radius: 20px;
+      overflow: hidden;
+      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(24, 33, 58, 0.95), rgba(18, 26, 47, 0.95));
+      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
+    }
+
+    .question {
+      width: 100%;
+      padding: 20px 22px;
+      border: 0;
+      background: transparent;
+      color: var(--text);
+      font: inherit;
+      display: flex;
+      align-items: center;
+      justify-content: space-between;
+      gap: 18px;
+      cursor: pointer;
+      text-align: left;
+    }
+
+    .question:hover,
+    .question:focus-visible {
+      background: rgba(140, 200, 255, 0.06);
+      outline: none;
+    }
+
+    .question span {
+      color: var(--accent);
+      font-size: 1.4rem;
+      line-height: 1;
+      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
+    }
+
+    .example.open .question span {
+      transform: rotate(45deg);
+    }
+
+    .details {
+      padding: 0 22px 22px;
+      color: var(--muted);
+      line-height: 1.7;
+    }
+
+    .details p {
+      margin: 0;
+    }
+
+    .details ul {
+      margin: 12px 0 0 20px;
+      padding: 0;
+    }
+
+    @media (max-width: 640px) {
+      .hero {
+        padding: 22px;
+        border-radius: 20px;
+      }
+
+      .question,
+      .details {
+        padding-left: 18px;
+        padding-right: 18px;
+      }
+    }
+  </style>
+</head>
+<body>
+  <main class="page">
+    <section class="hero" aria-label="FAQ introduction">
+      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
+      <h1>Everything you were curious about cats.</h1>
+      <p class="intro">Tap a question to expand its answer. Each cat fact is tucked away by default so the page stays clean, calm, and easy to scan.</p>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="faq" aria-label="Cat frequently asked questions">
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
+          Why do cats purr?
+          <span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" hidden>
+          <p>Cats often purr when they feel relaxed and safe, but they may also purr while seeking comfort, healing, or reassurance. It is one of their most expressive little sounds.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
+          How much sleep do cats need?
+          <span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" hidden>
+          <p>Most cats sleep 12 to 16 hours a day, and some kittens or older cats may sleep even more. Their napping schedule helps them conserve energy for short bursts of play and hunting behavior.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
+          Why do cats knead with their paws?
+          <span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" hidden>
+          <p>Kneading is a comforting behavior that often starts in kittenhood. Adult cats may knead when they are content, marking territory, or settling into a cozy spot.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
+          Do cats recognize their names?
+          <span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" hidden>
+          <p>Yes, many cats can recognize their names, even if they do not always choose to react. They often learn to associate the sound with attention, food, or other routines.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
+          Why do cats bring "gifts"?
+          <span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" hidden>
+          <p>Those surprise offerings are usually part instinct and part social behavior. Your cat may be sharing a catch, practicing hunting, or simply treating you like part of the pride.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+  </main>
+
+  <script>
+    document.querySelectorAll('.example').forEach((example) => {
+      const button = example.querySelector('.question');
+      const details = example.querySelector('.details');
+
+      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
+        const expanded = button.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
+        button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!expanded));
+        details.hidden = expanded;
+        example.classList.toggle('open', !expanded);
+      });
+    });
+  </script>
+</body>
+</html>
*** End Patch
